{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,200p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2131201979/13/prompt.md\"","aggregated_output":"你是一个 ARC-AGI 谜题设计专家。下面的 20 道参考题是难度和机制质量的标杆。仔细阅读每道题的**解题逻辑**（解题者从样例归纳规则的认知过程），而非表面场景。你的新题应在机制深度和隐蔽性上与参考题持平或者实现超越。\n\n每个参考题描述包含：\n- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\n- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\n- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\n- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\n\n参考题目如下：\n<reference_puzzle index=\"1\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"1a244afd\" lines=\"49-68\">\n<description>\nRotate each magenta source pixel 90 degrees counterclockwise around its matched blue pivot, recoloring the new pixel orange.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- The only foreground colors are blue pivot pixels and magenta source pixels.\n- Each magenta source can be paired one-to-one with a blue pivot in the same\n  row or column.\n\nRule:\n- Remove all magenta source pixels.\n- For each matched source/pivot pair, preserve the source distance from the\n  pivot but rotate its offset 90 degrees counterclockwise.\n- Paint the rotated in-bounds target orange; if the target is outside the\n  grid, the source simply disappears.\n\nKey insight:\nThe blue pixels are rotation centers, and row/column alignment gives a\nunique global matching from each magenta source to its pivot.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"2\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"1b59e163\" lines=\"54-69\">\n<description>\nCopy each marked sprite to every standalone marker of the same color and erase the original sources.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- Each source is an 8-connected component containing a monochrome sprite and one marker pixel of another color.\n- Other isolated marker pixels may be destinations; marker colors with no source sprite are distractors.\n\nRule:\n- Clear the grid to background.\n- For every source marker color, place the sprite at each other marker of that color using the source marker as the anchor.\n- Keep each destination marker pixel in place; do not keep source sprites, source markers, or distractor markers.\n\nKey insight:\n- A colored marker is not part of the sprite geometry; it is the anchor that says where same-colored copies of that sprite should be stamped.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"3\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"dc46ea44\" lines=\"11-25\">\n<description>\nMove the lower sprite and its pink guide into the upper panel, aligning the sprite to the guide's lower-left branch.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid has one dominant background color and one full-width separator row.\n- Below the separator are exactly two foreground roles: a five-pixel guide marker and one monochrome sprite.\n- The guide marker has normalized shape {(0,2), (1,2), (2,0), (2,2), (3,1)} and starts immediately below the separator.\n\nRule\n- Clear the canvas to the background, preserving the separator row.\n- Translate the guide marker upward so its top row becomes row 0.\n- Move the sprite, preserving its color and shape, so the sprite bbox bottom-right aligns to the translated guide's lower-left branch.\n\nKey insight\n- The marker supplies the destination anchor: its lower-left branch cell is where the moved sprite's bbox bottom-right must land.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"4\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"b99e7126\" lines=\"34-48\">\n<description>\nScale a minority cell's inner pattern up to the cell-grid level, completing a fractal overlay.\n\nInput structure:\n- Grid divided into NxN cells by separator lines of a single color.\n- Most cells share an identical interior pattern (majority); a few have a distinct pattern (minority).\n\nRule:\n- Extract the inner pixel pattern from the minority cell.\n- Treat each pixel as a cell-sized stamp: active pixels → minority pattern, inactive → majority pattern.\n- Position this scaled-up pattern on the cell grid so existing minority cells align with active pixels.\n- Fill in all remaining active positions with the minority pattern.\n\nKey insight: The minority cell's interior is a miniature blueprint of where minority cells should appear at the grid scale — fractal self-similarity.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"5\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"332f06d7\" lines=\"9-23\">\n<description>\nSlide a solid square through a winding channel to reach a same-sized target square.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg (most common color). A river color forms a winding corridor.\n- Two same-sized NxN solid squares on the river: mover and destination, each a distinct color.\n\nRule:\n- The mover square travels along the river toward the destination.\n- It can only pass through positions where the full NxN area is river.\n- If reachable, the mover replaces the destination; otherwise it stops at the farthest reachable point.\n- The mover's original position is filled with the river color.\n\nKey insight: Chokepoints narrower than N pixels block the square, forcing it to stop short.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"6\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"5ecac7f7\" lines=\"23-36\">\n<description>\nCombine the left, middle, and right ordered objects from three separated panels.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid is three HxH panels separated by one-cell vertical separator bars.\n- The background is the dominant color, and each panel contains exactly three same-color 4-connected foreground objects.\n\nRule\n- Build a new HxH background canvas.\n- From the left panel copy its leftmost object, from the middle panel copy its middle object, and from the right panel copy its rightmost object.\n\nKey insight\n- The separator bars create three aligned layers, and the panel's own left-to-right object order selects which object survives in the merged output.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"7\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"37ce87bb\" lines=\"33-47\">\n<description>\nCompute a grey result bar by adding teal bar heights and subtracting red bar heights.\n\nInput structure\n- The grid has a dominant background and several bottom-aligned one-cell-wide vertical bars.\n- Teal bars are positive operands; red bars are negative operands.\n- The penultimate column is an empty result slot.\n\nRule\n- Keep every input bar unchanged.\n- Compute result height = total teal bar height - total red bar height.\n- Paint that many bottom cells of the penultimate column grey.\n\nKey insight\n- The bars encode arithmetic by height, with color providing the sign.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"8\" source=\"train\" puzzle_id=\"99caaf76\" lines=\"56-75\">\n<description>\nMove each marked cross object away from its marker to the grid edge while rotating the colored cross 180 degrees.\n\nInput structure:\n- The background is the dominant color.\n- Each 8-connected foreground object has nine pixels: a 4-pixel marker-color\n  sprite attached to a 5-pixel non-marker colored cross.\n- Each object bbox is either 3x6 or 6x3, so the marker sprite is on exactly\n  one side of the cross.\n\nRule:\n- Move the whole object straight away from its marker side until the object\n  bbox touches the corresponding grid edge.\n- Keep the marker sprite unchanged within the object.\n- Rotate the 3x3 colored cross block by 180 degrees before placing it.\n\nKey insight:\nThe marker sprite is a directional tail; the cross is the leading payload,\nand only that payload turns around during the slide to the edge.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"9\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"de809cff\" lines=\"86-103\">\n<description>\nTurn black dents in two colored regions into marked opposite-color patches.\n\nInput structure:\n- Black background with two large foreground colors.\n- The large regions contain small black dents and a few one-cell color specks\n  or protrusions along region boundaries.\n\nRule:\n- Locally clean the two foreground regions: isolated specks become black, and\n  one-cell protrusions surrounded by the other region take that region's color.\n- Each original black dent whose cleaned 3x3 neighborhood is mostly one\n  foreground color becomes the center of a 3x3 patch in the opposite color.\n- The dent center itself is recolored teal (8).\n\nKey insight: The teal pixels mark the original black defects; the surrounding\n3x3 patch uses the other foreground color, after first removing boundary noise.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"10\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"a6f40cea\" lines=\"74-88\">\n<description>\nComplete partial paths inside a framed rectangle by projecting external color traces inward.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg, a 1px rectangular frame (border color) with uniform interior fill.\n- Colored components outside the frame touching its edges.\n\nRule:\n- Output = the frame's interior, filled with the fill color.\n- Map each outside component's frame-touch points into interior coordinates.\n- Monochrome components become solid Manhattan stripes between mapped endpoints.\n- Two-color components become alternating-color Manhattan paths.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
